==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* High combo potential.
* Very high damage.
* All moves are multi-target.
* All moves can damage [[enemies]] in [[Sea Events]].
*Very good for [[PvP]]  if used correctly.
* Great for grinding because of its high damage, fast [M1] attack speed, [[Area of Effect|AoE]], and no forward dash on [M1] attacks.

|'''[Z] Revolving Ravager'''
* Long stun if held.
* Big vertical hitbox.
* Great combo starter.
* Extends the enemy's hitbox, making the player capable of extending combos with short range moves.

|'''[X] Slayer of Goliath'''
* Great mobility.
* Very long range if held.
* Great combo potential.
* Bypasses some of [[Buddha]]'s defense and ignores [[Dragon]]'s defense buffs.
* The tap version can be used to punish players for missing their moves if the user has good aim since the tap version breaks Instinct if landed directly and has very little startup and endlag.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Hard to obtain, as the player needs both [[Tushita]] and [[Yama]], both swords with 350 mastery to start the [[Cursed Dual Katana/Puzzle|Cursed Dual Katana puzzle]], which is quite time-consuming on its own. [[Tushita]] requires [[rip_indra True Form]] spawned to start the puzzle for it.
* High mastery requirements.
* All moves are [[Instinct]] Trickable.
* A highly used sword, thus, very well known on how to counter.

|'''[Z] Revolving Ravager'''
* Not recommended for grinding, as the tornado does not drag multiple enemies when released. However, the explosion can hit multiple enemies.
* [[Instinct]] trickable.

|'''[X] Slayer of Goliath'''
* Small hitbox.
* Hard to hit moving opponents.
* The second explosion does not occur against multiple enemies. It can only occur to one enemy.
* Second highest mastery requirement for a skill in the game (375), behind death step (400).
* Players often trick Cursed Dual Katana users, as they wait the user to hold the entire X, and when the user travels to the target, they can get surprised by the opponent's sudden or instant moves (Like Ice's V).
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Cursed Dual Katana is often abbreviated as "CDK" by players.
* It is the only sword the [[Ghost]] '''[V] Ghostbusters''' clones are unable to use, due it being cursed to the user alone.
* The Cursed Dual Katana deals the fourth-highest damage per click out of every [[sword]] in the game (the third is [[True Triple Katana]], the second is [[Bisento]] V2, and the first is [[Triple Dark Blade]]).
* {{Ability|Z}} is as fast as [[Dark Blade]]'s {{Ability|Dark Blade|X}} move, but [[Dark Blade]]’s {{Ability|Dark Blade|X}} move has more range.
* {{Ability|X}} requires 375 [[Mastery]], the second-highest move mastery requirement in the game. Only [[Death Step]]'s {{Ability|Death Step|V}} is higher, at 400 Mastery.
** Despite this, once a player reaches [[Sea of Treats|Cake Land]], enemies yield relatively more mastery, making it easier to grind past this point.
** If timed perfectly, it is possible to [[Flash Step]] out of both moves.
* Using [[Godhuman]]'s {{Ability|Godhuman|Z}} move while the opponent is trapped inside the tornado from Cursed Dual Katana's {{Ability|Cursed Dual Katana|Z}} move will cause the move's animation to follow the opponent who is trapped inside the tornado.
* The Cursed Dual Katana was considered one of the best [[swords]] in the game by the community due to its versatility and attack power, but many more recent weapons outshine it in most fields.
* The Cursed Dual Katana, along with [[Shark Anchor]], are the only swords in the game that ignore [[Dragon]]'s defense buff.
** This is likely due to the One Piece counterpart, Enma, was the only sword to have ever cut Kaido, who the East Dragon variant was based off of.
* There was a  glitch that allowed the player to use {{Ability|X}} and immediately unequip the sword from their hotbar will freeze the target in place, rendering them unable to move until they die or switch teams. This has been patched on the Dragon Update.
* When the player is holding Cursed Dual Katana, it is noticeable that [[Yama]]'s handle has two small demonic wings flapping around, whereas [[Tushita]] has two small angelical wings flapping around; however, the animation is easily missable.
